  description: "For two and a half centuries the Hudson's Bay Company sat at the mouths of the rivers of Hudson Bay and James Bay and waited for the Omushkego Cree, the Eeyou Cree, the Dene and the Inuit to come down to it. This lesson follows the rivers to the bay, looks at the posts as meeting places with their own rules and their own troubles, and follows the surveyors who finally went up the rivers into the Barren Lands.",
